,"bbox":{"x0":0.086269841274241,"y0":0.32315174202070474,"x1":0.4684286323143941,"y1":0.3362970871160277},"ocr":false},{"page":1,"seq":10,"kind":"section_header","text":"Findings and treatment","bbox":{"x0":0.086269841274241,"y0":0.3551620040245554,"x1":0.28094647803222283,"y1":0.3700285584538834},"ocr":false},{"page":1,"seq":11,"kind":"text","text":"Physical examination revealed tenderness over the lateral aspect of the right ankle with mild swelling and limited range of motion. No deformity or instability was noted. X-ray of the ankle was performed and showed no evidence of fracture or dislocation. The patient was treated with ice, compression, and elevation, along with prescription of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory medication. The patient was advised to avoid weight-bearing activities and to follow up in one week for reassessment.","bbox":{"x0":0.086269841274241,"y0":0.3874212893102713,"x1":0.9052568085349632,"y1":0.4615009778239803},"ocr":false},{"page":1,"seq":12,"kind":"text","text":"Attending physician: Macario Vara Signature and stamp","bbox":{"x0":0.086269841274241,"y0":0.5077899962161792,"x1":0.2908667680917718,"y1":0.5188596538821916},"ocr":false}],"parser":"docling","seconds":0.31}
